<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oise (department)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oise is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the Hauts-de-France region, created in 1790 and named after the river Oise. Its prefecture is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beauvais">Beauvais</a>, and it includes Compiègne, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senlis">Senlis</a> and Chantilly. In ancient times its lands were home to the Gallic Bellovaci and Silvanectes, and they later formed part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ile-de-france">Île-de-France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oise-department.jpg" alt="Oise (department)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chatsam · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prefecture_beauvais_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
